<LegalPage
  title="Disclaimer"
  updated="24 July 2026"
  description="How to read what's on this site: information, not advice; no promised returns; off-plan risks stated plainly."
>
  <p>
    Renaissance &amp; Co. Investments provides advisory and information services relating to
    overseas real estate, with an initial focus on the United Arab Emirates. This page explains
    how to read everything else on the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Information, not advice</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing on this website is financial, investment, tax, or legal advice, and nothing here is a
    personal recommendation. We are not licensed financial advisors. Before you commit to any
    purchase, take independent professional advice — including from a qualified chartered
    accountant on the Indian tax and remittance treatment that applies to your situation.
  </p>

  <h2>No promised returns</h2>
  <p>
    We do not promise or guarantee returns, rental income, appreciation, or resale value. Property
    values move in both directions. As of the most recent verification, the Dubai market is in an
    orderly correction, and off-plan is the segment most exposed to it. Any figures shown on this
    site are indicative, are attributed to a source, and are dated to when they were verified; they
    can change after that date and should be re-checked before you rely on them.
  </p>

  <h2>Off-plan risks</h2>
  <p>Off-plan purchases carry specific risks you should plan for:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Handover dates can move; build the possibility of delay into your plan.</li>
    <li>What is delivered does not always match what was rendered or promised.</li>
    <li>If rental income is meant to cover instalments, budget for a vacancy gap.</li>
    <li>Off-plan is the segment a market correction reaches first.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Buyer protections exist — payments sit in independent escrow under UAE Law No. 8 of 2007, and
    the developer can draw against them only at verified construction milestones — but these reduce
    risk, they do not remove it.
  </p>

  <h2>On “tax-free” and residency</h2>
  <p>
    Where we describe UAE property as “tax-free,” we mean specifically that the UAE does not levy
    tax on rental income and has no personal income or capital gains tax. This says nothing about
    what you may owe in India. Separately, the UAE golden visa requires property valued near
    AED 2 million and is not linked to entry-level pricing; do not read one as implying the other.
  </p>

  <h2>Registration and partners</h2>
  <p>
    Registration of the entity is in progress. Nothing on this site should be taken as a claim of
    registered or licensed status. UAE transactions are completed through our exclusive UAE partner,
    Bellavierre, Dubai, which is a separate company.
  </p>

  <p class="note">
    Questions about anything on this page: [contact email — to be added]. We would rather you asked.
  </p>
